  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "寶石科學鑑定與人文賞析",
    "sub_ename": "THE SCIENTIFIC IDENTIFICATION AND HUMANISTIC APPRECIATION OF GEMSTONES",
    "describe_ch": "本課程教導學生瞭解鑽石寶石及翡翠和闐玉石等鑑定原理方法及各類寶石美學賞析，由授課老師提供鑽石翡翠和闐玉石及其他寶石如壽山石、雞血石等實品供同學鑑賞並解說各類寶石化學及礦石成分及實際樣品科學鑑定方法及寶石美學賞析並以較專業知識應用於鑽石、各類有色寶石及翡翠玉石之鑑定，並陪養學生除了本科系專業智能外，以寶石的美學陶冶學生內涵，並使學生在人文、藝術、社會與自然科學有均橫發展，並培養學生對地球資源永續利用的價值觀。本課程內容涵蓋：鑽石寶石及玉石鑑定之要領及方法概論學生修習本課程能陶冶心靈及對人文、美學提升，另鑽石的開採在非洲安哥拉、獅子山共和國等礦工的血淚，對非洲血鑽石開採工人的人權探討。",
    "describe_eh": "This course aims to teach the students to understand the fundamental characteristics of diamond gems and natural jadeite. The principles of identification methods of these precious gems will be taught as well. Meanwhile, the students are expected to learn appreciation of precious gems by the laboratory practical performance. The aesthetic of treasure stones could cultivate temperament of students. The students could have cross-disciplinary learning in the areas of humanities, arts, social and natural sciences. The laboratory performance contains identification methods for diamond, jadeite and other treasure stones such as shoushan stone and chicken blood stone. The laboratory performance tools used in identification of diamond and gems will be taught. Finally, students will learn the story of blood diamond, which are diamonds mined in war zones in Africa. Diamond has been sold to finance conflicts and thereby profit warload and these diamond companies around the world will be illustrated.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
  "targets": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "describe_ch": "鑽石及翡翠玉石及各種寶石真偽鑑定的原理，使用儀器與實作技術及流程。",
      "describe_en": "The identification methods of diamond gems and natural jadeite by laboratory performance techniques."
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "describe_ch": "以寶石美學陶冶學生內涵，啟蒙學生跨域學習人文藝術潛能。",
      "describe_en": "The aesthetic of treasure stones can cultivate humanities and arts temperament of students. The students could have cross-disciplinary learning and elicit the humanistic qualities and artistic creation."
    }
  ],
